  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 322 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nThrough Monday... \n\nAnother bout of showers are expected to develop over the Hattiesburg \narea, weak short-lived thunder can not be ruled out with these \nshowers. Some showers may extend west of HBG but lift and moisture \nin those areas remains more limited. As the diurnally driven showers \ndiminish overnight, thin patchy ground fog from saturated soils may \ndevelop in low lying areas during the early morning hours. No travel \nimpacts are expected with any fog that may develop as it will \nrapidly burn off with sunrise.  \n\nHigh pressure will settle over the Southeast CONUS over the course \nof this week, lingering through the rest of the week. Areawide \n\"Limited\" heat risk will continue to be advertised. Sites along and \nwest of I-55 are now advertised \"Elevated\" with heat indices \nexceeding 105 and reaching up to 110. As a result, a heat \nadvisory has been issued for those areas. As the high lingers \nover our area, cut-off low disturbances will traverse around the \nridge, bringing deep moisture and daily storm chances (25-50%) \nstarting along the HWY 84 corridor today and tomorrow. Mid-week, \nrain chances will expand into the I-20 corridor with heightened \nlift/moisture remaining throughout eastern MS as the pattern \nsettles in through the end of the week./OAJ/SW/",
